CONFIG_MACHINE_NAME
  The name shown in BIOS identification strings.

CONFIG_BIOS_BRAND
  Short brand name shown on the POST banner.

CONFIG_BIOS_STYLE_NAME
  Style name shown in the POST banner subtitle.

CONFIG_WEBSITE
  Website URL shown on the POST screen.

CONFIG_ROS_RELEASE
  ROS firmware release number (0-255).

CONFIG_ROS_ISSUE
  ROS firmware issue number (0-255).

CONFIG_BASE_MEMORY_KB
  Amount of conventional base memory in kilobytes.
  The PC1640 originally shipped with 640 KB, but some boards
  may have 608 KB (reserving top 32 KB for EMS).

CONFIG_HAS_PARADISE_PEGA1A
  Enable support for the onboard Paradise PEGA1A EGA controller
  found in the Amstrad PC1640.

CONFIG_HAS_AMSTRAD_MOUSE
  Enable support for the Amstrad-specific mouse interface.

CONFIG_HAS_BATTERY_BACKED_RTC
  Enable battery-backed real time clock support.

CONFIG_HAS_MATH_COPROCESSOR
  Report that an 8087 math coprocessor is installed.

CONFIG_COM1_BASE
  I/O base address for COM1 serial port.
  Standard value: 0x03F8.

CONFIG_COM2_BASE
  I/O base address for COM2 serial port.
  Standard value: 0x02F8.

CONFIG_LPT1_BASE
  I/O base address for LPT1 parallel port.
  Standard value: 0x0378.

CONFIG_LPT2_BASE
  I/O base address for LPT2 parallel port.
  Standard value: 0x03BC.

CONFIG_VIDEO_80X25_COLOR
  Use 80x25 color text as the default video equipment setting.

CONFIG_VIDEO_40X25_COLOR
  Use 40x25 color text as the default video equipment setting.

CONFIG_VIDEO_EGA_ADAPTER
  Use EGA adapter as the default video equipment setting.

CONFIG_VIDEO_MONO
  Use monochrome as the default video equipment setting.

CONFIG_VIDEO_ATTRIBUTE
  Default text attribute byte for POST display (hex).
  0x07 = normal white-on-black.

CONFIG_VIDEO_DIRECT_TEXT_INIT
  Perform direct text mode initialization before the PEGA option ROM
  is called. Required for correct display on PC1640 hardware.

CONFIG_VIDEO_USE_PC1640_SWITCH_BLOCK
  Read the PC1640 switch block to determine display configuration.

CONFIG_VIDEO_QUERY_ROM_STATE
  Query the video ROM for its current state after initialization.

CONFIG_VIDEO_FIXUP_FROM_SWITCH_BLOCK
  Apply video state fixups based on the PC1640 switch block settings.

CONFIG_VIDEO_OPTION_ROM_SCAN_ENABLED
  Scan for and execute video option ROMs in the C000-C7FF range.

CONFIG_OPTION_ROM_SCAN_ENABLED
  Scan for and execute non-video option ROMs in the C800-EFFF range.

CONFIG_HAS_FLOPPY_CONTROLLER
  Enable support for the onboard floppy disk controller.
  Disable this if no floppy controller is present and you want
  to boot exclusively from IDE.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_SUPPORT_35DD
  Enable support for 720K 3.5-inch DD floppy drives.
  If disabled, only 360K 5.25-inch DD drives are supported.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_A_NONE
  Drive A is not installed.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_A_360K
  Drive A is a 360K 5.25" DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_A_720K
  Drive A is a 720K 3.5" DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_B_NONE
  Drive B is not installed.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_B_360K
  Drive B is a 360K 5.25" DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_B_720K
  Drive B is a 720K 3.5" DD floppy drive.

CONFIG_FLOPPY_ENABLE_AH08_COMPAT
  Enable the INT 13h AH=08h (get drive parameters) compatibility
  path. Required by some DOS versions.

CONFIG_XTIDE_ENABLED
  Enable built-in IDE hard disk support compatible with XTIDE ISA
  adapters. This provides INT 13h services for ATA hard drives
  connected via an 8-bit ISA IDE controller at the configured
  I/O base address.

CONFIG_XTIDE_BASE
  I/O base address for the XTIDE IDE controller.
  Common values: 0x0300, 0x0320, 0x0340.

CONFIG_XTIDE_BOOT_ENABLED
  Allow the INT 19h bootstrap loader to attempt booting from
  the IDE hard drive after floppy boot fails.

CONFIG_XTIDE_PROBE_MASTER
  Probe for an IDE master device (drive 0) during POST.

CONFIG_XTIDE_PROBE_SLAVE
  Probe for an IDE slave device (drive 1) during POST.

CONFIG_XTIDE_PREFER_LBA
  Use LBA28 addressing with translated CHS geometry when the
  drive supports LBA. If disabled, native CHS is used.

CONFIG_XTIDE_TRANSLATED_HEADS
  Number of heads to report in translated CHS geometry (1-255).
  255 is typical for LBA translation.

CONFIG_XTIDE_TRANSLATED_SECTORS
  Number of sectors per track in translated CHS geometry (1-63).
  63 is typical for LBA translation.

CONFIG_XTIDE_POLL_LOOPS
  Number of polling iterations to wait for IDE status changes.
  Higher values increase timeout tolerance but slow detection
  of absent hardware. Minimum 256.

CONFIG_XTIDE_EDD_ENABLED
  Enable INT 13h extensions (Enhanced Disk Drive services) for
  LBA access. Required by modern operating systems.

CONFIG_XTIDE_EDD_MAX_BLOCKS
  Maximum number of sectors per EDD read/write request (1-127).

CONFIG_UART_INIT
  UART initialization byte written during serial port setup.
  0xE3 = 9600 baud, 8N1.

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_SECONDS
  Default RTC seconds value used when battery is dead (0-59).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_MINUTES
  Default RTC minutes value used when battery is dead (0-59).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_HOURS
  Default RTC hours value used when battery is dead (0-23).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_DAY_OF_MONTH
  Default RTC day of month used when battery is dead (1-31).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_MONTH
  Default RTC month used when battery is dead (1-12).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_YEAR
  Default RTC 2-digit year used when battery is dead (0-99).

CONFIG_RTC_DEFAULT_CENTURY
  Default RTC century used when battery is dead (19 or 20).

CONFIG_POST_PRETTY_WAIT_PANEL
  Show a formatted POST progress panel during boot.

CONFIG_POST_SPACE_INVADERS_SOUND
  Play a Space Invaders-style sound effect through the speaker
  during cold boot POST.

CONFIG_DEBUG_PORT_E9
  Route debug output to I/O port 0xE9 (Bochs/QEMU debug console).

CONFIG_DEBUG_COM1
  Route debug output to the COM1 serial port.

CONFIG_DEBUG_VIDEO_STATE
  Enable verbose tracing of video state changes.

CONFIG_DEBUG_VIDEO_OVERLAY
  Enable video debug overlay display.

CONFIG_TRACE_VIDEO_COM1
  Mirror video trace output to COM1.
